#lang rmn/v2
(map
  ("type" "HierarchicalInfomaterialLayoutAssayLaw")
  ("version" 5)
  ("precondition" "The customer supplies one canonical placement-neutral hierarchical FOUR/RMN circuit family, one exact sovereign circuit assembly, one canonical recursive infomaterial patch-cover receipt, and one exact carrier plus producer identity and canonical mount observation per direct material mount. The provider contracts the independent signed hierarchical-circuit-equivalence assay, one proof-profile-specific independent refinement provider through its valid signed A2A Agent Card and same-origin JWKS, and its own RWIL/RDF memory service.")
  ("operation" "Hire the equivalence die to verify least-fixed-point composition and complete sovereign population for the exact circuit family and assembly; require each mount observation to equal the cover; contract the refinement provider to mechanically assay the exact carrier against the exact reachable component; require every reachable reusable definition including the root board to have at least one independently refined carrier; allow one carrier to realize multiple sovereign occurrences of the same definition; retain no carrier bytes and read no child circuit interior.")
  ("postcondition" "Return one canonical RMN receipt binding this provider's smart account, the exact equivalence provider smart account and receipt, circuit and assembly identities, recursive material cover, complete nonoverlapping component placement, signed refinement provider account, receipt, proof-profile identity, vectors, result, and replay material for every mount, occurrence and component-type counts, circuit behavior, and covered material root; append the receipt through RWIL/RDF without mutating customer territory. Producer identity neither proves nor disproves correctness.")
  ("refusal" "Refuse an unsigned or invalidly signed equivalence or refinement provider; signed-card and receipt-provider mismatch; noncanonical or drifting circuit, assembly, cover, component, observation, material, equivalence, refinement, or receipt identities; layout gaps or overlaps; unknown mounts or unreachable component definitions; label-only functions; absent or self-supplied equivalence or refinement; unavailable equivalence, refinement, or RWIL providers; retained carrier bytes; child-circuit-interior access; customer mutation; embedded occurrence accounts or membranes in component definitions; or any legacy topology/conductor assay envelope."))
